<title>FINLAND: Municipality Finance sets FIM 150 mln 10-yr bond.</title>
<headline>Municipality Finance sets FIM 150 mln 10-yr bond.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond with step-up coupons and a call option in year five was announced by lead manager Unibank.</p>
<p> BORROWER    MUNICIPALITY FINANCE</p>
<p> AMT	   150 MLN MARKKA</p>
<p> COUPON	5.875 YEARS 1-5, 8.950 YEARS 6-10</p>
<p> MATURITY    18.SEPT.06</p>
<p> ISS PRICE   99.30</p>
<p> LAST MOODY  Aaa</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P    AAA</p>
<p>NOTES: The issuer has the right to call the bonds on 18 Sept 2001 giving 30 days notice. If not called, the coupon in years six to 10 is 8.950 percent.</p>
<p>The bonds will be issued to both Finnish and international investors, Unibank said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
